!! Verify wiki-only access

Tailscale permissions are additive. A narrow port-10000 rule does not restrict an existing broad allowance. Review rules covering `*` or `autogroup:shared` too; do not replace your whole existing policy with an example. Limit guest access to the host and TCP 10000. From an actual invited user's device, confirm the wiki is accessible but 443 and 8443 are not, while the owner's AI services still work. ForgeShare checks Serve configuration but cannot prove guests' effective access policy.

* [[Tailscale: sharing a machine and controlling access|https://tailscale.com/docs/features/sharing]]
* [[Tailscale grants|https://tailscale.com/docs/reference/syntax/grants]]
